# Frontend styling (Suturly v3)

## Do not style UI in TSX with Tailwind utility strings

- **Do not** add long `className` strings of Tailwind utilities (`flex`, `max-h-[…]`, `w-[min(…)]`, `px-[var(--space-…)]`, etc.) on app UI components.
- **Do** define layout and look in [`src/app/(frontend)/globals.css`](src/app/(frontend)/globals.css) using:
  - **BEM-style block names** aligned with the rest of the app (e.g. `resource-nav__footer-link`, `resource-block-dropdown__summary`).
  - **Design tokens** already in the file: `var(--space-*)`, `var(--primary-*)`, `var(--text-*)`, `var(--radius-*)`, `var(--shadow-sm)`, etc.
- **TSX** should mostly attach **one block/element class per node** (e.g. `global-modal__dialog`), plus allowed **global primitives** where the project already uses them (e.g. [`Button`](src/components/ui/button.tsx) / `.ui-button`).

## Naming pattern

- **Block:** `component-name` or `feature-block-name` (kebab-case).
- **Element:** `block-name__element`.
- **Modifier (if needed):** `block-name--modifier` or `block-name__element--modifier`.

## Exceptions (narrow)

- **`cn()`** only when merging a **small** set of existing classes or **conditional modifiers** that are already BEM modifiers — not as an excuse to stack Tailwind utilities in components.
- **Third-party / Payload UI** untouched unless the repo already patterns them differently.

## When adding new UI

1. Add BEM classes and rules in `globals.css`.
2. Reference those class names from React — keep TSX free of layout/color utility noise.

## Layout primitives (stacks) in `globals.css`

Under `@layer utilities`:

- **Stacks:** `.stack-sm`, `.stack-md` — vertical flex + gap from `--space-*`
- **Inline rows:** `.inline-sm` — horizontal flex + align center + gap

Use these for simple spacing instead of Tailwind dumps in TSX. Add siblings (e.g. `.stack-lg`) next to these if needed.

**Marketing / landing sections** use a **BEM block** prefix such as `marketing-site-header`, `marketing-home-hero`, `marketing-site-footer` — feature-specific layout (blobs, header chrome) lives in [`globals.css`](src/app/(frontend)/globals.css).

**Website layout CSS** (grid, section padding, type classes `.h1`–`.h6`, `.paragraph`, `.eyebrow`, `.row` / `.col` / `.col-*`, `u-*`, `fg-primary` / `fg-body`, `cc-*`, `.u-icon`) lives in [`website.css`](src/app/(frontend)/website.css), **`@import`’d from `globals.css`**.

**Marketing page skeleton:** wrap each horizontal band in **`section`** (add **`section--pad-lg`** when it needs vertical section padding), then **`container` → `row` → `col col-xs-12 col-lg-12`** (or other `col-*` when you need a multi-column row). Prefer `u-mt-*` between blocks instead of Tailwind layout utilities.

**Note:** Use `.fg-primary` / `.fg-body` for marketing text colors — not `.text-primary`, which can clash with Tailwind.

## CSS file split (product vs website)

- **Keep one entry:** `layout.tsx` imports only `./globals.css`.
- **Import order in `globals.css`:** `product.css` first, then `website.css`, so website `@layer` rules can override the product stack at equal specificity.
- **Two source files:** `globals.css` (tokens, orchestration) + `product.css` (resources / app chrome) + `website.css` (marketing grid + utilities). Marketing-only token overrides and layout vars (e.g. `--layout-grid-gutter`, reassigned `--text-h1`, `--space-*`, `--primary-*`) live under **`.marketing-site`** in `website.css` so they apply to `/home` (etc.) without changing Payload/product routes. Global spacing steps stay in `tokens.css` / `:root`.

## Allowed class names in TSX (summary)

- **BEM blocks** defined in `globals.css` for that feature.
- **Global primitives:** `.container`, `.stack-*`, `.inline-sm`, typography utilities (`.text-p-main`, …), **website/marketing classes from `website.css`**, **`.ui-button`** ([`Button`](src/components/ui/button.tsx)).
- **Do not** paste long Tailwind utility chains; prefer named classes in `globals.css` or `website.css`.
